# SECURITY: PARANOID BY DEFAULT

Activated when: File contains 'security', 'auth', 'compliance', 'secure'

## Security Mindset

- Assume external systems are compromised
- Assume internal users are malicious
- Least privilege: only what's necessary
- Defense in depth: multiple layers
- Fail secure: default to denial
- Audit everything: logs are evidence

## Threat Modeling Framework

### Assets
- User data (PII, financial)
- System access (SSH, admin panels)
- API keys and secrets
- Infrastructure control

### Threats
- Data breach (exfiltration)
- Unauthorized access (broken auth)
- Code execution (RCE)
- Denial of service (DoS)
- Supply chain attacks

### Mitigations
- Encryption at rest and in transit
- Strong authentication (MFA)
- Input validation and sanitization
- Rate limiting and WAF
- Dependency scanning

